1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:09,080
The brush clears a river barge, loaded with grain. In the Mauryan empire, rivers carried tax grain and tribute to the capital.

2
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:17,256
An empire this big needed officers, spies and records. How do you run an empire without roads or phones?

3
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:41,931
How do we know? The Arthashastra describes an ideal state. Megasthenes describes what he saw at the capital.

4
00:00:41,931 --> 00:00:49,073
And Ashoka's edicts name officers. Each source has limits, so historians compare them.

5
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:13,860
The Arthashastra describes the state as having seven limbs: the king, the ministers, the territory, the fort, the treasury, the army and the ally.

6
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:17,988
The king stood at the top, advised by a council of ministers.

7
00:01:17,988 --> 00:01:24,680
Under them were officers called adhyakshas, who ran departments, such as trade, mines and weights.

8
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:34,988
The empire was split into provinces, ruled by princes or governors. Taxila, Ujjain, Tosali and Suvarnagiri were the main centres.

9
00:01:34,988 --> 00:01:41,583
Below them were districts and villages. Spies, called gudhapurushas, kept the king informed.

10
00:01:41,583 --> 00:01:47,188
Megasthenes says the city of Pataliputra was run by six committees of five members each.

11
00:01:47,188 --> 00:01:52,996
The chief tax on farmers was the bhaga, a share of the harvest, often given as one sixth.

12
00:01:52,996 --> 00:02:02,107
The state also owned mines, forests and some farms. The army was large, with infantry, cavalry, chariots and elephants.

13
00:02:02,107 --> 00:02:07,332
Greek writers give very large numbers, which may be exaggerated.

14
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:26,557
Scholars disagree. How tightly did the Mauryas rule?

15
00:02:26,557 --> 00:02:34,835
One view says the state was highly centralised, with many officers and strong control, as the Arthashastra and Megasthenes suggest.

16
00:02:34,835 --> 00:02:41,887
Another view says control was strong at the centre and looser at the edges, resting on local chiefs and distance.

17
00:02:57,083 --> 00:03:06,184
Carve this tip into memory. Seven limbs, six committees. one-sixth share. Seven, six and one-sixth.

18
00:03:06,184 --> 00:03:09,293
Three numbers that anchor the Mauryan state.

19
00:03:24,483 --> 00:03:40,657
Dig Quiz. Pause and name it. Number one. How many limbs does the Arthashastra give the state? The answer: seven. Number two.

20
00:03:40,657 --> 00:03:56,761
Name the chief land tax of the Mauryas. The answer: the bhaga. Number three. What were the royal spies called?

21
00:03:56,761 --> 00:04:06,116
The answer: gudhapurushas. Now one line for Mains. Discuss the nature of Mauryan administration.

22
00:04:25,317 --> 00:04:34,322
The barge goes into its case. Rivers carried the wealth of the state. Three facts to take away. A river barge for tax grain.

23
00:04:34,322 --> 00:04:42,649
Seven limbs of the state. Bhaga: a share of the harvest. Next gallery: Ashoka and the Dhamma.

